module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.BaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.DenseSubsiteModules
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.AffineSubsite
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.InverseImage.AbelianSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Module.Localization.Exactness

/-!
# Quasi-coherent presheaves of modules on the affine crystalline site are sheaves

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)` and let `AffineCris(X/S)` be the affine
crystalline site of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/SmallSite/AffineSubsite.lean`,
ringed by the restriction `𝒪` of the structure sheaf of `Cris(X/S)`, whose sections over an
object `(U, T, δ)` are `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)`.  Let `N` be a presheaf of `𝒪`-modules on `AffineCris(X/S)`.
For a morphism `k : A ⟶ B` there is the base change of sections
`𝒪(A) ⊗_{𝒪(B)} N(B) ⟶ N(A)`, `r ⊗ x ↦ r • N(k)(x)`.  This file proves that **if every such base
change map is bijective, then `N` is a sheaf**, and packages `N` as a sheaf of modules.

The proof is Zariski descent for modules.  The topology of `AffineCris(X/S)` is generated by the
families of restrictions `B|_{D(r_i)} ⟶ B` of an object to the basic opens of a family `(r_i)`
of global sections of its (affine) ambient scheme generating the unit ideal: such a family is a
Zariski covering, and conversely every Zariski covering family of `B` is refined by one, since
the basic opens form a basis of the topology of an affine scheme.  Over such a family the
sections of `𝒪` over `B|_{D(r)}` are the localization `𝒪(B)_r`, so the bijectivity of the base
change maps says that `N(B|_{D(r)})` is the localization `N(B)_r`, and the sheaf condition is
the exactness of `0 → N(B) → ∏ N(B)_{r_i} → ∏ N(B)_{r_i r_j}`, which is
`IsLocalizedModule.Away.injective_pi_and_exact_of_span_range_eq_top` ([Stacks, Tag 00EK]).

## Main definitions

Everything below lives in the namespace `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`.

* `affineStructureSheaf` — the sheaf of rings `𝒪` of `AffineCris(X/S)`, the restriction of the
  structure sheaf of `Cris(X/S)` along the inclusion.
* `affineRingAlong k` — the sections of `𝒪` over the source of a morphism `k`, as an algebra over
  the sections over its target through the restriction map of `k`.
* `affineBaseChange N k` — the base change of sections `𝒪(A) ⊗_{𝒪(B)} N(B) ⟶ N(A)` along
  `k : A ⟶ B`.
* `basicOpenCoverage` — the coverage of `AffineCris(X/S)` by restrictions to standard basic open
  covers of the ambient schemes.
* `sheafOfBijectiveAffineBaseChange` — a presheaf of modules all of whose base change maps are
  bijective, as a sheaf of modules on `AffineCris(X/S)`.

## Main results

* `isLocalizedModule_affineRestrictAlong` — when the base change map along the restriction to a
  basic open `D(r)` is bijective, the restriction map `N(B) ⟶ N(B|_{D(r)})` is a localization
  away from `r`.
* `basicOpenCoverage_toGrothendieck` — the standard basic open covers generate the topology of
  `AffineCris(X/S)`.
* `isSheaf_of_bijective_affineBaseChange` — **a presheaf of modules on `AffineCris(X/S)` whose
  base change maps are all bijective is a sheaf.**  The variant
  `isSheaf_of_bijective_affineBaseChange_basicOpen` asks this only for the restrictions to basic
  opens.

## Implementation notes

The `𝒪(B)`-algebra structure on `𝒪(A)` depends on the morphism `k : A ⟶ B`, so it is carried by
the type synonym `affineRingAlong k`, which has `k` in its type, as
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.ringAlong` does on the big site; likewise the sections
`N(A)` regarded as an `𝒪(B)`-module through `k` are the synonym `affineModuleAlong N k`.  The
base change map is then Mathlib's `LinearMap.liftBaseChange`, and the bijectivity hypothesis is
literally Mathlib's `IsBaseChange`, which `isLocalizedModule_iff_isBaseChange` turns into a
localization of modules.  The ring `Γ(T, D(r))` is the localization of `Γ(T, ⊤)` away from `r`
by Mathlib's instance `AlgebraicGeometry.Γ_restrict_isLocalization`, which applies on the nose
because the ambient scheme of the restriction of `(U, T, δ)` to an open `V` of `T` is the open
subscheme `V` and its structure morphism the open immersion of `V`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00EK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00EK)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

noncomputable section

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

variable {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}}

/-- **The structure sheaf `𝒪` of the affine crystalline site `AffineCris(X/S)`**: the restriction
of the structure sheaf of `Cris(X/S)` along the inclusion `AffineCris(X/S) ⥤ Cris(X/S)`.  Its
sections over an object `(U, T, δ)` are `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)`. -/
abbrev affineStructureSheaf (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    Sheaf (affineTopology S) RingCat.{u} :=
  Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.ringRestriction (affineTopology S) (smallTopology S) (affineι S)
    (structureSheaf S)

/-- The ring of sections of the structure sheaf `𝒪` of `AffineCris(X/S)` over an object
`(U, T, δ)`, which is the ring `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)`. -/
abbrev affineSectionRing (A : AffineCrystallineThickening S) : Type u :=
  (affineStructureSheaf S).obj.obj (op A)

/-- The sections of `𝒪` over an object of `AffineCris(X/S)` form a commutative ring, the ring of
global sections of its ambient scheme. -/
instance instCommRingAffineSectionRing (A : AffineCrystallineThickening S) :
    CommRing (affineSectionRing A) :=
  inferInstanceAs (CommRing Γ(A.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤))

/-- The restriction map `𝒪(B) ⟶ 𝒪(A)` of the structure sheaf of `AffineCris(X/S)` along a
morphism `k : A ⟶ B`. -/
abbrev affineSectionMap {A B : AffineCrystallineThickening S} (k : A ⟶ B) :
    affineSectionRing B →+* affineSectionRing A :=
  ((affineStructureSheaf S).obj.map k.op).hom

/-- **The sections of `𝒪` over the source of a morphism `k : A ⟶ B` of `AffineCris(X/S)`**,
carrying the `𝒪(B)`-algebra structure given by the restriction map of `k`.  The synonym carries
`k` in its type so that this structure, which depends on `k`, can be an instance. -/
def affineRingAlong {A B : AffineCrystallineThickening S} (_k : A ⟶ B) : Type u :=
  affineSectionRing A

/-- **The sections of a presheaf of modules `N` over the source of a morphism `k : A ⟶ B` of
`AffineCris(X/S)`**, carrying the `𝒪(B)`-module structure obtained by restricting scalars along
the restriction map of `k`. -/
def affineModuleAlong (N : PresheafOfModules.{u} (affineStructureSheaf S).obj)
    {A B : AffineCrystallineThickening S} (_k : A ⟶ B) : Type u :=
  N.obj (op A)

variable (N : PresheafOfModules.{u} (affineStructureSheaf S).obj)
  {A B : AffineCrystallineThickening S} (k : A ⟶ B)

/-- The commutative ring structure of `affineRingAlong k`, that of `𝒪(A)`. -/
instance instCommRingAffineRingAlong : CommRing (affineRingAlong k) :=
  inferInstanceAs (CommRing (affineSectionRing A))

/-- `𝒪(A)` as an `𝒪(B)`-algebra through the restriction map of `k : A ⟶ B`. -/
instance instAlgebraAffineRingAlong : Algebra (affineSectionRing B) (affineRingAlong k) :=
  (affineSectionMap k).toAlgebra

/-- The additive group of `affineModuleAlong N k`, that of `N(A)`. -/
instance instAddCommGroupAffineModuleAlong : AddCommGroup (affineModuleAlong N k) :=
  inferInstanceAs (AddCommGroup (N.obj (op A)))

/-- `N(A)` as a module over `affineRingAlong k`, its own `𝒪(A)`-module structure. -/
instance instModuleAffineRingAlongAffineModuleAlong :
    Module (affineRingAlong k) (affineModuleAlong N k) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Module (affineSectionRing A) (N.obj (op A)))

/-- `N(A)` as an `𝒪(B)`-module, by restriction of scalars along the restriction map of `k`. -/
instance instModuleAffineModuleAlong : Module (affineSectionRing B) (affineModuleAlong N k) :=
  Module.compHom (N.obj (op A)) (affineSectionMap k)

/-- The two scalar actions on `affineModuleAlong N k` are compatible. -/
instance instIsScalarTowerAffineModuleAlong :
    IsScalarTower (affineSectionRing B) (affineRingAlong k) (affineModuleAlong N k) where
  smul_assoc b t x := mul_smul (affineSectionMap k b) (show affineSectionRing A from t)
    (show N.obj (op A) from x)

/-- `N(A)` as a module over `affineRingAlong k`, its own `𝒪(A)`-module structure; this is the
action in which the base change map `affineBaseChange N k` is linear. -/
instance instModuleAffineRingAlong : Module (affineRingAlong k) (N.obj (op A)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Module (affineSectionRing A) (N.obj (op A)))

/-- The restriction map `N(B) ⟶ N(A)` of a presheaf of modules along `k : A ⟶ B`, as an
`𝒪(B)`-linear map. -/
def affineRestrictAlong : N.obj (op B) →ₗ[affineSectionRing B] affineModuleAlong N k where
  toFun x := N.restrictₛₗ k.op x
  map_add' x y := map_add (N.restrictₛₗ k.op) x y
  map_smul' b x := (N.restrictₛₗ k.op).map_smulₛₗ b x

/-- `affineRestrictAlong N k` sends `x` to its restriction `N(k)(x)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem affineRestrictAlong_apply (x : N.obj (op B)) :
    affineRestrictAlong N k x = N.restrictₛₗ k.op x :=
  rfl

/-- **The base change of sections of a presheaf of modules `N` along a morphism `k : A ⟶ B` of
`AffineCris(X/S)`**: the `𝒪(A)`-linear map `𝒪(A) ⊗_{𝒪(B)} N(B) ⟶ N(A)`, `r ⊗ x ↦ r • N(k)(x)`,
where `𝒪(A)` is an `𝒪(B)`-algebra through the restriction map of `k`. -/
def affineBaseChange :
    affineRingAlong k ⊗[affineSectionRing B] N.obj (op B) →ₗ[affineRingAlong k] N.obj (op A) :=
  (affineRestrictAlong N k).liftBaseChange (affineRingAlong k)

/-- `affineBaseChange N k` sends `r ⊗ x` to `r • N(k)(x)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem affineBaseChange_tmul (r : affineRingAlong k) (x : N.obj (op B)) :
    affineBaseChange N k (r ⊗ₜ x) = r • N.restrictₛₗ k.op x :=
  rfl

/-- The restriction map of a presheaf of modules along a morphism `ρ : Z' ⟶ Z` over `B`, as an
`𝒪(B)`-linear map between the sections regarded as `𝒪(B)`-modules through the two morphisms to
`B`. -/
def affineTransferAlong {Z Z' : AffineCrystallineThickening S} {k : Z ⟶ B} {k' : Z' ⟶ B}
    (ρ : Z' ⟶ Z) (hρ : ρ ≫ k = k') :
    affineModuleAlong N k →ₗ[affineSectionRing B] affineModuleAlong N k' where
  toFun x := N.restrictₛₗ ρ.op x
  map_add' x y := map_add (N.restrictₛₗ ρ.op) x y
  map_smul' b x := by
    subst hρ
    have e : affineSectionMap (ρ ≫ k) b = affineSectionMap ρ (affineSectionMap k b) := by
      rw [affineSectionMap, affineSectionMap, affineSectionMap, op_comp, Functor.map_comp,
        RingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.comp_apply]
    show N.restrictₛₗ ρ.op (affineSectionMap k b • @id (N.obj (op Z)) x) =
      affineSectionMap (ρ ≫ k) b • @id (N.obj (op Z')) (N.restrictₛₗ ρ.op x)
    rw [LinearMap.map_smulₛₗ, e]
    rfl

/-- Restricting along `k` and then along `ρ` is restricting along `ρ ≫ k`. -/
theorem affineTransferAlong_comp {Z Z' : AffineCrystallineThickening S} {k : Z ⟶ B}
    {k' : Z' ⟶ B} (ρ : Z' ⟶ Z) (hρ : ρ ≫ k = k') :
    (affineTransferAlong N ρ hρ).comp (affineRestrictAlong N k) = affineRestrictAlong N k' := by
  subst hρ
  ext x
  show N.map ρ.op (N.map k.op x) = N.map (ρ ≫ k).op x
  rw [op_comp, N.map_comp_apply]

/-- The ambient scheme of an object of `AffineCris(X/S)` is affine. -/
private theorem isAffine_target (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S) :
    IsAffine B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme :=
  B.property.2

namespace AffineCrystallineThickening

/-- A basic open of the ambient scheme of an object of `AffineCris(X/S)` is affine. -/
theorem isAffineOpen_basicOpen (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S)
    (r : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) :
    IsAffineOpen (B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme.basicOpen r) :=
  have := isAffine_target B
  (isAffineOpen_top _).basicOpen r

/-- The restriction of an object of `AffineCris(X/S)` to the basic open `D(r)` of its ambient
scheme defined by a global section `r`, an object of `AffineCris(X/S)`. -/
abbrev restrictBasicOpen (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S)
    (r : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) : AffineCrystallineThickening S :=
  restrictOpen B.obj (isAffineOpen_basicOpen B r)

/-- The structure morphism `B|_{D(r)} ⟶ B` of the restriction to a basic open. -/
abbrev restrictBasicOpenHom (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S)
    (r : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) : restrictBasicOpen B r ⟶ B :=
  restrictOpenHom B (isAffineOpen_basicOpen B r)

end AffineCrystallineThickening

open AffineCrystallineThickening

/-- **The sections of `𝒪` over the restriction of an object of `AffineCris(X/S)` to a basic open
`D(r)` are the localization of the sections over the object away from `r`.**  The ambient scheme of
the restriction is the open subscheme `D(r)` of an affine scheme. -/
instance isLocalization_restrictBasicOpen (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S)
    (r : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) :
    IsLocalization.Away (show affineSectionRing B from r)
      (affineRingAlong (restrictBasicOpenHom B r)) := by
  haveI : IsAffine B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme := B.property.2
  exact Γ_restrict_isLocalization _ r

/-- **When the base change map along the restriction to a basic open `D(r)` is bijective, the
restriction map `N(B) ⟶ N(B|_{D(r)})` is a localization away from `r`.**  Bijectivity says that
`N(B|_{D(r)})` is the base change of `N(B)` to `𝒪(B)_r`. -/
theorem isLocalizedModule_affineRestrictAlong (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S)
    (r : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤))
    (h : Function.Bijective (affineBaseChange N (restrictBasicOpenHom B r))) :
    IsLocalizedModule.Away (show affineSectionRing B from r)
      (affineRestrictAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B r)) := by
  rw [IsLocalizedModule.Away, isLocalizedModule_iff_isBaseChange (Submonoid.powers _)
    (affineRingAlong (restrictBasicOpenHom B r))]
  exact IsBaseChange.of_equiv (LinearEquiv.ofBijective _ h) fun x ↦
    one_smul (affineRingAlong (restrictBasicOpenHom B r))
      (affineRestrictAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B r) x)

/-- **The coverage of `AffineCris(X/S)` by standard basic open covers**: the covering presieves of
an object `B` are the families of restrictions `B|_{D(r_i)} ⟶ B` to the basic opens of a family
`(r_i)` of global sections of its ambient scheme generating the unit ideal.  A family pulls back
along `g : A ⟶ B` to the family defined by the images of the `r_i` in the sections over `A`. -/
def basicOpenCoverage (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    Coverage (AffineCrystallineThickening S) where
  coverings B := {R | ∃ (I : Type (u + 1)) (f : I → Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)),
    Ideal.span (Set.range f) = ⊤ ∧
      R = Presieve.ofArrows (fun i ↦ restrictBasicOpen B (f i))
        fun i ↦ restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i)}
  pullback := by
    rintro B A g R ⟨I, f, hf, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨Presieve.ofArrows
      (fun i ↦ restrictBasicOpen A (g.hom.hom.targetHom.hom.appTop (f i)))
      fun i ↦ restrictBasicOpenHom A (g.hom.hom.targetHom.hom.appTop (f i)), ⟨I, _, ?_, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    · change Ideal.span (Set.range (g.hom.hom.targetHom.hom.appTop.hom ∘ f)) = ⊤
      rw [Set.range_comp, ← Ideal.map_span, hf, Ideal.map_top]
    · rintro Z k ⟨i⟩
      obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := CrystallineThickening.exists_comp_restrictOpenHom_eq_of_le g.hom
        (B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme.basicOpen (f i))
        (A.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme.basicOpen (g.hom.hom.targetHom.hom.appTop (f i)))
        (Scheme.preimage_basicOpen_top _ _).ge
      exact ⟨restrictBasicOpen B (f i), ObjectProperty.homMk p, restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i), ⟨i⟩,
        ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ hp⟩

/-- The family of restrictions to the basic opens of a family of sections generating the unit
ideal is a covering presieve of `basicOpenCoverage`. -/
theorem ofArrows_mem_basicOpenCoverage (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S) {I : Type (u + 1)}
    (f : I → Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) (hf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = ⊤) :
    Presieve.ofArrows (fun i ↦ restrictBasicOpen B (f i)) (fun i ↦ restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i)) ∈
      basicOpenCoverage S B :=
  ⟨I, f, hf, rfl⟩

/-- Sections generate the unit ideal iff the basic opens they define cover the ambient scheme. -/
private theorem span_range_eq_top_iff_forall_exists_mem_basicOpen
    (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S) {I : Type*}
    (f : I → Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range f) = ⊤ ↔
      ∀ x : B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme,
        ∃ i, x ∈ B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme.basicOpen (f i) := by
  have := isAffine_target B
  rw [← (isAffineOpen_top _).self_le_iSup_basicOpen_iff, SetLike.le_def]
  simp

/-- **The standard basic open covers generate the topology of `AffineCris(X/S)`.**  A standard
basic open cover is a Zariski covering, and every Zariski covering family of an object is refined
by one: around each point of the affine ambient scheme there is a basic open contained in the
image of a member of the family, over which that member restricts to an isomorphism. -/
theorem basicOpenCoverage_toGrothendieck (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    (basicOpenCoverage S).toGrothendieck = affineTopology S := by
  refine le_antisymm (((Coverage.gi (AffineCrystallineThickening S)).gc _ _).2
    fun B R hR ↦ ?_) ?_
  · obtain ⟨I, f, hf, rfl⟩ := hR
    have := isAffine_target B
    exact affineZariskiCovering_mem_affineTopology S
      (restrictOpenCover B _ fun i ↦ isAffineOpen_basicOpen B (f i))
      (isZariskiCovering_restrictOpenCover B _ _
        ((span_range_eq_top_iff_forall_exists_mem_basicOpen B f).mp hf))
  · show (affinePrecoverage S).toGrothendieck ≤ _
    rw [Precoverage.toGrothendieck_eq_sInf]
    refine sInf_le ?_
    rintro B R ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩
    have := isAffine_target B
    have hcart : ∀ i, Thickening.IsCartesian (E.f i).hom.hom := hE.1
    have hE2 := hE.2
    simp only [Thickening.targetPresieve, Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff] at hE2
    have hoi : ∀ i, IsOpenImmersion (E.f i).hom.hom.targetHom.hom := fun i ↦ hE2.2 i
    have hpt : ∀ x : B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ (i : E.I₀)
        (r : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)),
        x ∈ B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme.basicOpen r ∧
          ∀ z ∈ B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme.basicOpen r,
            z ∈ Set.range (E.f i).hom.hom.targetHom.hom.base := by
      intro x
      obtain ⟨i, y, hy⟩ := hE2.1 x
      have := hoi i
      have hxV : x ∈ (E.f i).hom.hom.targetHom.hom.opensRange := ⟨y, hy⟩
      obtain ⟨r, hr, hxr⟩ :=
        (isAffineOpen_top B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme).exists_basicOpen_le
          (V := (E.f i).hom.hom.targetHom.hom.opensRange) ⟨x, hxV⟩ trivial
      exact ⟨i, r, hxr, fun z hz ↦ hr hz⟩
    choose i r hxr hr using hpt
    refine Coverage.mem_toGrothendieck_sieves_of_superset _ ?_ (ofArrows_mem_basicOpenCoverage B
      (fun x : ULift.{u + 1} B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme ↦ r x.down) ?_)
    · rintro Z k ⟨x⟩
      have := hoi (i x.down)
      have hle : B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme.basicOpen (r x.down) ≤
          (E.f (i x.down)).hom.hom.targetHom.hom.opensRange := fun z hz ↦ hr x.down z hz
      obtain ⟨Y, a, b, hb, fac⟩ := CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenHom_opensRange_mem_generate
        (E.f (i x.down)).hom (hcart _) (R := (E.map (affineι S)).presieve₀) ⟨i x.down⟩
      rcases hb with ⟨j⟩
      refine ⟨E.X j, ObjectProperty.homMk
        (CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenLE B.obj hle ≫ a), E.f j, ⟨j⟩,
        ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ ?_⟩
      show (CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenLE B.obj hle ≫ a) ≫
        (E.map (affineι S)).f j = _
      rw [Category.assoc, fac]
      exact CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom B.obj hle
    · exact (span_range_eq_top_iff_forall_exists_mem_basicOpen B _).mpr fun x ↦ ⟨⟨x⟩, hxr x⟩

namespace AffineCrystallineThickening

/-- The morphism `B|_{D(rs)} ⟶ B|_{D(r)}` between restrictions to basic opens. -/
def basicOpenMulLeft (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S)
    (r s : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) :
    restrictBasicOpen B (r * s) ⟶ restrictBasicOpen B r :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenLE B.obj
    (by rw [Scheme.basicOpen_mul]; exact inf_le_left))

/-- The morphism `B|_{D(rs)} ⟶ B|_{D(s)}` between restrictions to basic opens. -/
def basicOpenMulRight (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S)
    (r s : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) :
    restrictBasicOpen B (r * s) ⟶ restrictBasicOpen B s :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenLE B.obj
    (by rw [Scheme.basicOpen_mul]; exact inf_le_right))

/-- The morphism `B|_{D(rs)} ⟶ B|_{D(r)}` is a morphism over `B`. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem basicOpenMulLeft_restrictBasicOpenHom (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S)
    (r s : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) :
    basicOpenMulLeft B r s ≫ restrictBasicOpenHom B r = restrictBasicOpenHom B (r * s) :=
  ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom B.obj _)

/-- The morphism `B|_{D(rs)} ⟶ B|_{D(s)}` is a morphism over `B`. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem basicOpenMulRight_restrictBasicOpenHom (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S)
    (r s : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) :
    basicOpenMulRight B r s ≫ restrictBasicOpenHom B s = restrictBasicOpenHom B (r * s) :=
  ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom B.obj _)

end AffineCrystallineThickening

/-- **A presheaf of modules whose base change maps along restrictions to basic opens are bijective
satisfies descent for every standard basic open cover.**  The sections over the members of the
cover and over their pairwise intersections are localizations of the sections over the object, so
this is the exactness of `0 → N(B) → ∏ N(B)_{r_i} → ∏ N(B)_{r_i r_j}`, [Stacks, Tag 00EK]. -/
theorem isSheafFor_basicOpenCover (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S) {I : Type (u + 1)}
    (f : I → Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)) (hf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = ⊤)
    (h : ∀ r : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤),
      Function.Bijective (affineBaseChange N (restrictBasicOpenHom B r))) :
    Presieve.IsSheafFor (N.presheaf ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat.{u})
      (Presieve.ofArrows (fun i ↦ restrictBasicOpen B (f i))
        fun i ↦ restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i)) := by
  have hloc : ∀ r : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤),
      IsLocalizedModule.Away (show affineSectionRing B from r)
        (affineRestrictAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B r)) := fun r ↦
    isLocalizedModule_affineRestrictAlong N B r (h r)
  let g : ∀ i, N.obj (op B) →ₗ[affineSectionRing B]
      affineModuleAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i)) := fun i ↦
    affineRestrictAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i))
  let l : ∀ i j, affineModuleAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i)) →ₗ[affineSectionRing B]
      affineModuleAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i * f j)) := fun i j ↦
    affineTransferAlong N (basicOpenMulLeft B (f i) (f j))
      (basicOpenMulLeft_restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i) (f j))
  let r : ∀ i j, affineModuleAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B (f j)) →ₗ[affineSectionRing B]
      affineModuleAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i * f j)) := fun i j ↦
    affineTransferAlong N (basicOpenMulRight B (f i) (f j))
      (basicOpenMulRight_restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i) (f j))
  have hl : ∀ i j,
      (l i j).comp (g i) = affineRestrictAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i * f j)) :=
    fun i j ↦ affineTransferAlong_comp N _ _
  have hr : ∀ i j,
      (r i j).comp (g j) = affineRestrictAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i * f j)) :=
    fun i j ↦ affineTransferAlong_comp N _ _
  have : ∀ i, IsLocalizedModule.Away (show affineSectionRing B from f i) (g i) :=
    fun i ↦ hloc (f i)
  have : ∀ i j, IsLocalizedModule.Away
      ((show affineSectionRing B from f i) * (show affineSectionRing B from f j))
      ((l i j).comp (g i)) := fun i j ↦ by
    rw [hl i j]
    exact hloc (f i * f j)
  obtain ⟨hinj, hexact⟩ := IsLocalizedModule.Away.injective_pi_and_exact_of_span_range_eq_top
    (f := fun i ↦ (show affineSectionRing B from f i)) g l r hf
    fun i j ↦ (hl i j).trans (hr i j).symm
  rw [Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff]
  intro x hx
  let y : ∀ i, affineModuleAlong N (restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i)) := x
  have hcompat : ∀ i j, l i j (y i) = r i j (y j) := fun i j ↦
    hx i j (restrictBasicOpen B (f i * f j)) (basicOpenMulLeft B (f i) (f j))
      (basicOpenMulRight B (f i) (f j))
      ((basicOpenMulLeft_restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i) (f j)).trans
        (basicOpenMulRight_restrictBasicOpenHom B (f i) (f j)).symm)
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := (hexact y).mp (funext fun p ↦ by
    simp only [LinearMap.pi_apply, LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.proj_apply,
      Pi.zero_apply]
    exact sub_eq_zero.mpr (hcompat p.1 p.2))
  exact ⟨m, fun i ↦ congrFun hm i, fun t ht ↦
    hinj ((funext fun i ↦ ht i : LinearMap.pi g t = y).trans hm.symm)⟩

/-- **A presheaf of modules on `AffineCris(X/S)` whose base change maps along the restrictions to
basic opens are bijective is a sheaf.**  The sheaf condition for a presheaf of abelian groups is
that of its underlying presheaf of sets, which need only be checked on the standard basic open
covers, `basicOpenCoverage_toGrothendieck`. -/
theorem isSheaf_of_bijective_affineBaseChange_basicOpen
    (h : ∀ (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S) (r : Γ(B.obj.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤)),
      Function.Bijective (affineBaseChange N (restrictBasicOpenHom B r))) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (affineTopology S) N.presheaf := by
  refine CategoryTheory.Sites.AbelianSheaf.isSheaf_of_forget (affineTopology S) N.presheaf ?_
  rw [CategoryTheory.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type]
  refine Presieve.isSheaf_of_le _ (basicOpenCoverage_toGrothendieck S).ge ?_
  rw [Presieve.isSheaf_coverage]
  rintro B R ⟨I, f, hf, rfl⟩
  exact isSheafFor_basicOpenCover N B f hf (h B)

/-- **A presheaf of modules on the affine crystalline site `AffineCris(X/S)` all of whose base
change maps `𝒪(A) ⊗_{𝒪(B)} N(B) ⟶ N(A)` are bijective is a sheaf.**  Only the base change maps
along restrictions to basic opens are used, `isSheaf_of_bijective_affineBaseChange_basicOpen`. -/
theorem isSheaf_of_bijective_affineBaseChange
    (h : ∀ {A B : AffineCrystallineThickening S} (k : A ⟶ B),
      Function.Bijective (affineBaseChange N k)) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (affineTopology S) N.presheaf :=
  isSheaf_of_bijective_affineBaseChange_basicOpen N fun B r ↦ h (restrictBasicOpenHom B r)

/-- **A presheaf of modules on `AffineCris(X/S)` all of whose base change maps are bijective, as a
sheaf of modules**, by `isSheaf_of_bijective_affineBaseChange`. -/
def sheafOfBijectiveAffineBaseChange
    (h : ∀ {A B : AffineCrystallineThickening S} (k : A ⟶ B),
      Function.Bijective (affineBaseChange N k)) :
    SheafOfModules.{u} (affineStructureSheaf S) :=
  ⟨N, isSheaf_of_bijective_affineBaseChange N h⟩

/-- The underlying presheaf of modules of `sheafOfBijectiveAffineBaseChange N h` is `N`. -/
@[simp]
theorem sheafOfBijectiveAffineBaseChange_val
    (h : ∀ {A B : AffineCrystallineThickening S} (k : A ⟶ B),
      Function.Bijective (affineBaseChange N k)) :
    (sheafOfBijectiveAffineBaseChange N h).val = N :=
  rfl

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

